{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc","id":138687,"title":"Another Round at GMC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T18:25:24-07:00","id":138687,"title":"Another Round at GMC","content":"Hey.<br /> I'm alive.<br /> Also, done.<br /> (Except for Transmutations. Fuck that).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Check it out.</a><br /> <br /> Thank you:<br /> - Verge, for all the help last year. Suuuuper grateful I had someone as knowledgeable as you to bounce ideas with.<br /> - Kingsraven, for making me really think about this.<br /> - Eremite, for all your input and a good part of the Torment system I put in here.<br /> - DataWeaver, for providing a ton of critique, insight and smrts.<br /> <br /> I'm running (like, actually running a game) with these rules. I've said that like, three times now? One of them fell apart. The other one got put on hiatus. So one Promethean game with these rules isn't so bad; at this moment, everyone thinks these look pretty solid.<br /> <br /> I welcome critique and insight. So far, this has all been working well.<br /> <br /> I am worried about<b></b>:<br /> - Conditions I made. Want to check for balance. I think the resolutions are fun.<br /> - Copyright. Blackhatmatt made the Wasteland stuff, and I only changed around some things (and made it all in one place); I hacked up most of the Disquiet stuff on my own, and the Torment section is based mostly off of Eremite's hack (which is, uh. Somewhere. I'll link it if anyone finds it).<br /> - Not being finished? I probably skipped some stuff. I have a lot of the &quot;ground-rules&quot; written up in other places, and my group understands implicitly (through my ranting and raving, of course) how these hacks work. If you find something and you're all &quot;hey this isn't actually explained,&quot; just let me know. I'll edit it in (and 1,000 apologies). I'll try to catch all of the trouble-spots soon.<br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> - I'm leaving the Experience Costs as they are. Transmutations are not something I'm going to re-write; I find the system bearable, so I'm re-working issues (and power levels) as I find them.<br /> - Speaking of: any comments about Transmutations or suggested hacks to them would be great.<br /> - I'd love input on the System Hacks section too; super boring down there right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:07:18-07:00","id":138783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc#post138687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey.<br /> I'm alive.<br /> Also, done.<br /> (Except for Transmutations. Fuck that).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Check it out.</a><br /> <br /> Thank you:<br /> - Verge, for all the help last year. Suuuuper grateful I had someone as knowledgeable as you to bounce ideas with.<br /> - Kingsraven, for making me really think about this.<br /> - Eremite, for all your input and a good part of the Torment system I put in here.<br /> - DataWeaver, for providing a ton of critique, insight and smrts.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Homer Simpson&gt;I am so smrt! I am so smrt!&lt;/Homer&gt; :P<br /> <br /> Seriously, glad I could help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc#post138687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running (like, actually running a game) with these rules. I've said that like, three times now? One of them fell apart. The other one got put on hiatus. So one Promethean game with these rules isn't so bad; at this moment, everyone thinks these look pretty solid.<br /> <br /> I welcome critique and insight. So far, this has all been working well.<br /> <br /> I am worried about<b></b>:<br /> - Conditions I made. Want to check for balance. I think the resolutions are fun.<br /> - Copyright. Blackhatmatt made the Wasteland stuff, and I only changed around some things (and made it all in one place); I hacked up most of the Disquiet stuff on my own, and the Torment section is based mostly off of Eremite's hack (which is, uh. Somewhere. I'll link it if anyone finds it).<br /> - Not being finished? I probably skipped some stuff. I have a lot of the &quot;ground-rules&quot; written up in other places, and my group understands implicitly (through my ranting and raving, of course) how these hacks work. If you find something and you're all &quot;hey this isn't actually explained,&quot; just let me know. I'll edit it in (and 1,000 apologies). I'll try to catch all of the trouble-spots soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t worry about the copyright stuff, as long as you attribute your sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc#post138687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notes:<br /> - I'm leaving the Experience Costs as they are. Transmutations are not something I'm going to re-write; I find the system bearable, so I'm re-working issues (and power levels) as I find them.<br /> - Speaking of: any comments about Transmutations or suggested hacks to them would be great.<br /> - I'd love input on the System Hacks section too; super boring down there right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll look things over and get back to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:04:54-07:00","id":139235,"title":"","content":"Nice work Ben Quo on this update! It's elegant and simple, yet it corrects a lot of what was wronged in the original edition. I think it's a nice addition that our patchwork friends now take only bashing damage from weapons, even though it renders the Clayflesh transmutation pretty useless. I'd rule it that bullets now deal a single point of bashing damage, and magical bullets now deal bashing damage instead of lethal.<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone that worked on this rewrite, I'll be using it real soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: I just realized you have not included the rules for beacons. You talk about how to complete them, modifiers to them but not the basics of them. What are they? How do you get them? etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 05-16-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:40:48-07:00","id":139740,"title":"","content":"So far I'm on page 4; and my first thought. This <u>really</u> needs a clear summery of just what &quot;adopted&quot; conditions are; both mechanically and fluff. It would be best if it appeared before the big chart.<br /> <br /> I shall now continue reading. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Your praise was really flattering!<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm down to witnesses; I think that the dice pool to gain a breaking point through witnessing should depend upon the severity of the sin. Seeing murder and people's reactions should make it obvious that it's bad. Seeing complex emotional abuse will just confuse a Promethian. It won't tie 1:1 with severity, but as a rough representation it should work.<br /> <br /> Another thought: A quashamallim should be able to create a beacon or create an additional breaking point. For example, in the Promethian Corebook an angel told Mr Varney that if he stays put he'll learn useful information. That could easily be represented by a new beacon. A different quashamallim might show up after a promethian hurts someone and hurt him in tun; then it says &quot;it's called pain, humans feel it&quot;. New adopted breaking point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Overall thought. If you used different styles of bullet point for different levels of indentation it would be more readable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Torment: I'm a big believer in reworking Torment significantly. A Promethean should always be in Torment, and the specific moments where you fail a roll and bad things happen should be called Release. For example for a Golem it's psychological torment to not be working, they crave work like addicts need drugs. Being somebody's tool is a freedom from that omnipresent pain, but Disquiet means that it always ends in a rampage. (You shut down your higher thought patterns in order to be a tool, then don't turn them back on until after you get attacked and retaliate)<br /> <br /> <br /> I was disapointed that Burdens never appeared. I really liked the idea of Burden conditions representing physical or supernatural weaknesses that vanish as the Promethean becomes more human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-16-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T10:44:16-07:00","id":140709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139235#post139235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice work Ben Quo on this update! It's elegant and simple, yet it corrects a lot of what was wronged in the original edition. I think it's a nice addition that our patchwork friends now take only bashing damage from weapons, even though it renders the Clayflesh transmutation pretty useless. I'd rule it that bullets now deal a single point of bashing damage, and magical bullets now deal bashing damage instead of lethal.<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone that worked on this rewrite, I'll be using it real soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the kind words <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Took a long time. Definitely proud of it.<br /> <br /> I'm still combing Transmutations. I'll check out Clayflesh and add an adjustment; it'll most likely be the one you suggested. Thanks ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139235#post139235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I just realized you have not included the rules for beacons. You talk about how to complete them, modifiers to them but not the basics of them. What are they? How do you get them? etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, yeah. That sounds like something I'd do. I edited it in.<br /> <br /> In short, Beacons are a person/place/thing that guide the Promethean towards mortality. They replace Milestones. Think of them like a second set of Aspirations; if you pick &quot;Dr. George Evans&quot; as a Beacon, then you're probably fascinated with healers, medicine, saving lives; you want to understand disease and ailment; you want to help people or know what it means to help someone or figure out why the strong humans bother to care for the weak.<br /> <br /> Instead of your Storyteller picking Milestones for you, you pick Beacons and work up to the &quot;Milestone Moment&quot; which is that confrontation detailed in the doc.<br /> Resolving a Beacon basically means incorporating some part of it into your nascent self - hence why you adopt a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Should I add anything else to that explanation/got any questions about it still?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T21:54:26-07:00","id":142074,"title":"","content":"I'll probably get to read it in a few months' time, but thanks for the shout-out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:18:49-07:00","id":147589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far I'm on page 4; and my first thought. This <u>really</u> needs a clear summery of just what &quot;adopted&quot; conditions are; both mechanically and fluff. It would be best if it appeared before the big chart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added. I'll expand upon it as I go. Knew something was missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Your praise was really flattering!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well<br /> It was true.<br /> I really appreciate constructive criticism; yours helped a lot. Testing has proved these fairly playable thus far; would have been less so without the aid ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down to witnesses; I think that the dice pool to gain a breaking point through witnessing should depend upon the severity of the sin. Seeing murder and people's reactions should make it obvious that it's bad. Seeing complex emotional abuse will just confuse a Promethian. It won't tie 1:1 with severity, but as a rough representation it should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The bare-ness of it was just so I could get it done and out; I've added a modifier table for samples.<br /> Initially, I was going to go with &quot;you must gain X successes based on the Humanity level of the Breaking Point,&quot; but I wasn't sure what to do with X. Having it be something like 3 to 5 x Humanity was going to be too easy at low levels, and ridiculously hard at Humanity 8 to 10; I didn't want it to be (7 + Humanity Rating) either.<br /> I'm more comfortable with a flat 10 and modifiers to the roll itself.<br /> Advice or suggestions for modifiers is welcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought: A quashamallim should be able to create a beacon or create an additional breaking point. For example, in the Promethian Corebook an angel told Mr Varney that if he stays put he'll learn useful information. That could easily be represented by a new beacon. A different quashamallim might show up after a promethian hurts someone and hurt him in tun; then it says &quot;it's called pain, humans feel it&quot;. New adopted breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deal.<br /> It's funny, I had a Burden that was basically this in the old draft. Dunno why I forgot about it.<br /> I'll probably actually call it &quot;Burden.&quot; Heh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall thought. If you used different styles of bullet point for different levels of indentation it would be more readable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> It's ugly.<br /> Legibility was second priority. Which I am working on now ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torment: I'm a big believer in reworking Torment significantly. A Promethean should always be in Torment, and the specific moments where you fail a roll and bad things happen should be called Release. For example for a Golem it's psychological torment to not be working, they crave work like addicts need drugs. Being somebody's tool is a freedom from that omnipresent pain, but Disquiet means that it always ends in a rampage. (You shut down your higher thought patterns in order to be a tool, then don't turn them back on until after you get attacked and retaliate)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down with this idea too, but I'd want to take Humanity in a different direction where I to do this.<br /> I like Torment as being a mechanic similar to (but longer than) Frenzy/Death Rage. My basic understanding of Torment - since <i>so many things</i> prompt it - is that it kind of is the default stage for a Promethean. They <i>are</i> always resisting it; the call is so strong to be less than a human.<br /> I'd be interested in seeing other versions, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=139740#post139740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was disapointed that Burdens never appeared. I really liked the idea of Burden conditions representing physical or supernatural weaknesses that vanish as the Promethean becomes more human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, too, but I ultimately rejected them because of personal time constraints (I work a lot. Not near a computer. Sigh) and a general wish to get some distance from that part of the project.<br /> <br /> An idea I'm playing with is making Burdens something you pick three of at character creation; one minor, one major, one superlative, and the amount of effect it has on you is based on the level (so a minor Patchwork Body would be more present but a less severe penalty than a superlative iteration of the same Burden). <br /> You'd shed them bit by bit, so as you go through the Pilgrimage you'd be able to downgrade the big ones and get rid of the little ones (all the while gaining Vitriol from them).<br /> <br /> It'd be a fairly lengthy project, though; I'd rather spend the time making Azothic Radiance something more before tackling Burdens again.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you were right: Beacons are a much better mechanism for advancing the Pilgrimage than Burdens (though you could work them in together, so every few Beacons you resolve - or don't - you get to work off a Burden).<br /> <br /> If I were feeling really ambitious (I am, actually, I just don't have a lot of time), I'd make Torment something personal to each Promethean; it has three components, one from Lineage and two you choose, and those components are your Burdens. Their penalties are ever-present but mild outside of Torment; in Torment, they ramp up. That way, every Lineage has a Torment that looks similar, but the rest of it is unique.<br /> If I work on that project I'll start posting it. It'd be big. Again, I'd rather toy with Azothic Radiance and Transmutations first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:56:53-07:00","id":147636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147589#post147589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Added. I'll expand upon it as I go. Knew something was missing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nice. I'd add something like<br /> <br /> Adopted Breaking Points at or above your current Humanity level protect you from Degeneration and are a requirement to increase your humanity.<br /> <br /> Between the 2nd and 3rd point on the current chart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147589#post147589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. The bare-ness of it was just so I could get it done and out; I've added a modifier table for samples.<br /> Advice or suggestions for modifiers is welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div> My advice would be to try and imagine how long it <i>should</i> take a Promethian to figure out various things are wrong by watching people's reactions; and then adjust the mechanics until they will probably get it in the correct number of rolls.<br /> <br /> So if you think people's horrified reactions to murder should be bloody obvious to a Promethian, it should require roughly one third of the dicepool in successes. I would say I'm pro-variable success numbers; as 10 means that everything will take quite a few examples to figure out while some things are just more confusing than others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147589#post147589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deal.<br /> It's funny, I had a Burden that was basically this in the old draft. Dunno why I forgot about it.<br /> I'll probably actually call it &quot;Burden.&quot; Heh.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd call it Baecons to avoid creating preconceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147589#post147589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down with this idea too, but I'd want to take Humanity in a different direction where I to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I just meant changing the name, and some fluff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147589#post147589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea I'm playing with is making Burdens something you pick three of at character creation; one minor, one major, one superlative, and the amount of effect it has on you is based on the level (so a minor Patchwork Body would be more present but a less severe penalty than a superlative iteration of the same Burden).</div> </div> </div> </div> That could work. Though I can think of some Burdens that might only work at certain levels.<br /> <br /> Asimov Compliant for example. That could be a cool Burden; if one you have to fix in the first session or two.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I did intend it to be alongside your Beacons rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> just a few Conditions that grant Vitriol and get resolved along the Pilgramage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T23:48:30-07:00","id":147678,"title":"","content":"I was going to suggest another name for Beacons, but then the imagery of a Promethean as a ship at sea struggling its way through rocks and following lighthouses sort of leapt out at me.<br /> <br /> Cannot unsee. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T00:54:24-07:00","id":147701,"title":"","content":"I wrote the Flying Dutchman as a Promethean crewed ship once.<br /> <br /> [edit] Having read Burdens a couple of thoughts.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I wouldn't worry so much about ridgid mechanics. Rather than rules saying how many Breaking Points and where they go; or the requirement for Torment or a Wasteland; just let the angels do what they like. You can trust the storyteller not to do anything silly, and it fits the established themes that Qashmallim do whatever the Principle wants; even break the rules.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the bit about how if a Promethian sheds a Qashmallim-given Breaking Point doesn't quite capture the mysteriousness of the Principle. If a Promethean abandons it's new Breaking Point, the Qashmallim might be thinking &quot;just as planned&quot;. Or it might have completed it's mission as soon as it gave the burden and no longer be around to know or care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-24-2014, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T04:50:36-07:00","id":147773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147678#post147678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to suggest another name for Beacons, but then the imagery of a Promethean as a ship at sea struggling its way through rocks and following lighthouses sort of leapt out at me.<br /> <br /> Cannot unsee. Well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you ^^<br /> It went through a few drafts. Points of light on a lonely road won out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T04:52:26-07:00","id":147774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=147701#post147701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote the Flying Dutchman as a Promethean crewed ship once.<br /> <br /> [edit] Having read Burdens a couple of thoughts.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I wouldn't worry so much about ridgid mechanics. Rather than rules saying how many Breaking Points and where they go; or the requirement for Torment or a Wasteland; just let the angels do what they like. You can trust the storyteller not to do anything silly, and it fits the established themes that Qashmallim do whatever the Principle wants; even break the rules.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the bit about how if a Promethian sheds a Qashmallim-given Breaking Point doesn't quite capture the mysteriousness of the Principle. If a Promethean abandons it's new Breaking Point, the Qashmallim might be thinking &quot;just as planned&quot;. Or it might have completed it's mission as soon as it gave the burden and no longer be around to know or care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never thought about the &quot;just as planned' angle. Angel. Angel angle.<br /> I am on-board with this idea.<br /> <br /> The guidelines were more suggestions, honestly; if I saw something like this in a book, I'd want a bit of a crash-course in how to use it. I'll edit it.<br /> <br /> I thought about it not being around. I decided to flub that anyway. I blame poor judgement from being tired (obviously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:29:44-07:00","id":148394,"title":"","content":"Update:<br /> - Re-read the doc. Added clarification, cleaned up errors and style.<br /> - Added &quot;Virtue and Vice&quot; to the Rules Hack section, and an idea called &quot;roadmarks&quot; that I'm fairly keen on. Have a look-see if you want.<br /> - Eyeing Transmutations. Distastefully, might I add. I guess when no tasks are left &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T05:37:38-07:00","id":148632,"title":"","content":"If you'd like I may start and rewrite some transmutations for the GMC update. You may then choose to take and use them or to tell me that these were not the transmutations you were looking for :P<br /> <br /> I'll have to do it anyways since I have a GMC promethean game coming soon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T07:32:51-07:00","id":148683,"title":"","content":"BTW, have you read The Golem and the Djinn? Great Promethean inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:16:56-07:00","id":148704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148632#post148632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'd like I may start and rewrite some transmutations for the GMC update. You may then choose to take and use them or to tell me that these were not the transmutations you were looking for :P<br /> <br /> I'll have to do it anyways since I have a GMC promethean game coming soon</div> </div> </div> </div>I've added a bunch of Transmutation changes to the bottom of the doc now. Nothing major yet.<br /> Well, talk with me homie: how do you want to change Transmutations?<br /> I'm down with the idea of removing dot-ratings from them, having them have pre-requisite Transmutations, and making them all a flat cost; BUT that would require fusing certain ones (like a bunch of the one-dot ones, which would end up being too weak) and altering the more powerful ones.<br /> <br /> I can probably finish them by myself at this point; I cruised through a bunch last night. It was easier than I thought it would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148632#post148632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, have you read The Golem and the Djinn? Great Promethean inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not. Clearly, I must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:56:10-07:00","id":148726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148704#post148704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, talk with me homie: how do you want to change Transmutations?<br /> I'm down with the idea of removing dot-ratings from them, having them have pre-requisite Transmutations, and making them all a flat cost; BUT that would require fusing certain ones (like a bunch of the one-dot ones, which would end up being too weak) and altering the more powerful ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the important point is to make them feel different from the other splat powers. People suggested doing Embeds/Exploits with transmutations but I feel like it would take a bite out of demon AND promethean by having them both work their powers in similar ways. I have no suggestion as of now to solve this problem. Might work on something soon. I for one think that some transmutations ought to be more obvious and dangerous-looking. Maybe one way to make transmutations interesting would be by creating a 3 tier power-level? Like &quot;Neophyte &lt; Apprentice &lt; Master&quot;. We could either work them as a 3 level power system (imagine &quot;glitches&quot;/embed/exploits) or more along the line of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fists of Talos</b><br /> At Neophyte level, the promethean is able to ignore (azoth) dots of durability from items he punches or strikes.<br /> At Apprentice level, [copy the Battering ram Transmutation]<br /> At Master level, promethean ignores durability completely and a single point of damage destroys the item. Magic items have no durability but their full structure.<br /> <br /> This Transmutation affects objects up to twice the size of the Promethean. </div> </div> </div>Also, despite the bad reviews and s***mouthing about the movie, my gaming group and I believe that &quot;I, Frankenstein&quot; is a very good promethean inspiration. It just came out in DVD so you'll probably be able to rent it. It does not deserve and oscar, but it's a very good story about a promethean caught in the Angel/Demon war of the god-machine. Also, everybody in this movie is apparently able to strike agravated damage at every turn. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:50:05-07:00","id":148746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148726#post148726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the important point is to make them feel different from the other splat powers. People suggested doing Embeds/Exploits with transmutations but I feel like it would take a bite out of demon AND promethean by having them both work their powers in similar ways. I have no suggestion as of now to solve this problem. Might work on something soon. I for one think that some transmutations ought to be more obvious and dangerous-looking. Maybe one way to make transmutations interesting would be by creating a 3 tier power-level? Like &quot;Neophyte &lt; Apprentice &lt; Master&quot;. We could either work them as a 3 level power system (imagine &quot;glitches&quot;/embed/exploits) or more along the line of this:</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor --&gt; Major --&gt; Superlative, to mimic Milestones (which by the way I no longer use; everything in the doc supplants those. I should probably add that in &gt;_&gt;).<br /> <br /> I like that. I mean:<br /> 1. It makes every power you purchase a mini-road<br /> 2. It means you have to purchase Transmutations in order, but they still have prerequisites, which are now inherent in each of them;<br /> 3. It actually drastically cuts down on Transmutation overlap and useless-ness, since the ones that - honestly, kind of suck - can now simply be combined and ramped-up into the lower ranks of a much broader, more useful tree.<br /> 4. I'd push to leave room for 1 to 5 dot powers, so my Might, Perfected Reflexes and Hard Body re-writes can be used).<br /> 5. It also makes pricing uniform.<br /> <br /> ALL THAT SAID I'm still just going to go through and adjust the ones from RAW, keeping the system the same, while you + myself + whoever hacks out a new Transmutation system.<br /> I'd rather have them all looked at and working, flawed (or non-ideal) as the current system is, then stop that and work on a whole new project. Also, if I finish adjusting them all for GMC-era power + rules, it'll be that much easier to cluster them into groups of 3 for a system-remake.<br /> OOOO and that'd make it easier to make Synergies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S.: Part of why I kept saying &quot;I don't want to do Transmutations&quot; was because the last time I did power-hacking? It was for Exalted, it was the Solar and the Abyssal Charmsets (in their entirety), and I basically worked on them night and day for two months.<br /> I'm going to be hyper-focusing on powers now. Bloody. ADHD. WHY<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148726#post148726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, despite the bad reviews and s***mouthing about the movie, my gaming group and I believe that &quot;I, Frankenstein&quot; is a very good promethean inspiration. It just came out in DVD so you'll probably be able to rent it. It does not deserve and oscar, but it's a very good story about a promethean caught in the Angel/Demon war of the god-machine. Also, everybody in this movie is apparently able to strike agravated damage at every turn. Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I - have negative feelings about Underworld, which I watched a lot of. I'll keep the recommendation in mind. Maybe the next time B-movie night rolls around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T15:26:56-07:00","id":148977,"title":"","content":"For Transmutations; I'd kinda like to capture both the divinity of the Fire, and the wrongness of patchwork corpses being the guys in charge of it.<br /> <br /> No clue how to do that though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T20:25:40-07:00","id":149100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=148977#post148977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Transmutations; I'd kinda like to capture both the divinity of the Fire, and the wrongness of patchwork corpses being the guys in charge of it.<br /> <br /> No clue how to do that though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well<br /> Flashing your Disfigurements - which promptly makes everyone check for Disquiet - pretty much screams &quot;wrongness&quot; to me. Divinity of Fire? We can probably make that evident with whatever the &quot;five-dot&quot; equivalent ends up being.<br /> As I go through them, some of the end-level Transmutations are fairly out there in these terms; others are - a little lacking.<br /> <br /> Transmutations grabbed me early-on as being a grab-bag-ish combination of other splat's powers; this is good and bad, you know?<br /> Ramping up the general power level should lead to more avenues for unique expression.<br /> <br /> A Promethean PC flashed her disfigurements in a police station last session, battling a Pandoran that unfolded from a two-way mirror (which promptly ate a cop, might I add). It was pretty badass to see a monster fight a monster.<br /> Nobody thought either of them were &quot;right.&quot;<br /> <br /> (She's an Ulgan. &quot;Horrific&quot; is a good adjective)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T02:27:26-07:00","id":149238,"title":"","content":"I think I have an idea.<br /> <br /> Fireflashes!<br /> <br /> <br /> Create a bunch of Conditions and/or drawbacks that a player can voluntarily add to their power for extra dice and/or successes. These effects should be power-of-god things.<br /> <br /> For example if a Promethian uses Arc, they could say that after hurting the target the lightning bolt jumps to a nearby corpse or inanimate object; bestowing life upon it for a scene. Pandora's book has a section on Firestorm aspects that could be adapted for Fireflashes. I'm sure the Bible will also have some neat possibilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, while I'm here. Here's a freebie.<br /> <br /> Shock<br /> <br /> Minor: The Promethean may charge his body with lightning, frying his opponents with a touch. By spending a point of Pyros the Promethian's next attack with his fists counts as though it were a weapon which does one damage. If the Promethean prefers he channel the electricity through a conductive weapon, increasing it's damage rating by one. All weapons enhanced by this Transmutation take (the Transmuation's damage - the weapon's Durability) point of damage to their structure each turn.<br /> <br /> All damage inflicted by electricity bypasses armour, unless it has the ability to protect against electricity. (N.B, with a few word changes it should work fine for Irradiation's attack power - just don't call it Blast)<br /> <br /> Major: The Promethean may now choose between a damage rating of one or three when using Shock. She may also use Shock at range, literally shooting lightning bolts from her body. This counts as a ranged weapon with a range of Azoth * 10 feet, a medium range of Azoth * 20 feet, and a long range of Azoth * 40 feet.<br /> <br /> In addition the Promethian gains the ability to lace their Shock based attacks with the essence of Torment. If they elect to do so then their electricity will bypass a Promethean's natural ability to heal from electricity, but not the protection granted by Insulator. Calling upon the power of Torment causes it to build within the Promethian, if she does this more than Humanity times in a single scene it becomes unbearable; she yearns for, and must roll to prevent, Release.<br /> <br /> Superlative: The Promethian may now choose between a damage rating of one, three of five when using Shock, and by spending a point of Willpower she may make the damage Aggravated. In addition, by spending an additional point of Pyros he may use the autofire rules with Shock based attacks. If he uses a conductive weapon to channel a melee attack, then the weapon's damage rating only applies to the first target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-26-2014, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:15:19-07:00","id":149556,"title":"","content":"Quick question to you TKR: if the fists of the promethean counts as a weapon, I understand it deals lethal damage?<br /> <br /> Also, kudos for the quick writing, exactly what I had in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:32:06-07:00","id":149561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149556#post149556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question to you TKR: if the fists of the promethean counts as a weapon, I understand it deals lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's correct.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:05:27-07:00","id":149613,"title":"","content":"I'd probably actually name each level; &quot;Shock/Arc/Divine Lightning,&quot; of course, since they clearly are that.<br /> If not, I'd probably name the whole thing &quot;Divine Lightning&quot; instead of &quot;Shock.&quot; One has that certain coolness to it.<br /> <br /> I'm a huge geek. I envision it being something like:<br /> <br /> <i>Electrificaiton Transmutations</i><br /> &quot;Sweet quote about lightning/divinity.&quot;<br /> Fancy words explaining the major pew-pew you're about to buy into.<br /> <br /> <i>Shock - Minor</i><br /> <b>Requirement: </b>None<br /> Words go here.<br /> <br /> <i>Arc - Major</i><br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Shock<br /> Words.<br /> <br /> <i>Divine Lightning - Supernal</i><br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Arc<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> This was obviously quick to write, which is good. It cleans up and cleaves pretty closely to the originals, too, which is important. Nice clean work ^^<br /> <br /> I'm on &quot;Metamorphosis&quot; right now. Magnum Opus and I are going to start tossing together this new system soon too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 05-26-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:36:13-07:00","id":149666,"title":"","content":"Here's a quote used in Genius: the Transgression. It's more metaphorical than literal:<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is the lightning to lick you with its tongue? Where is the madness with which you should be cleansed?<br /> Behold, I show you the Superman. He is this lightning, he is this madness.&quot;<br /> -Friedrich Nietzsche, Thus Spoke Zarathustra<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T12:47:21-07:00","id":149674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149613#post149613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably actually name each level; &quot;Shock/Arc/Divine Lightning,&quot; of course, since they clearly are that.<br /> <i>Electrificaiton Transmutations</i><br /> &quot;Sweet quote about lightning/divinity.&quot;<br /> Fancy words explaining the major pew-pew you're about to buy into.<br /> <br /> <i>Shock - Minor</i><br /> <b>Requirement: </b>None<br /> Words go here.<br /> <br /> <i>Arc - Major</i><br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Shock<br /> Words.<br /> <br /> <i>Divine Lightning - Supernal</i><br /> <b>Requirement:</b> Arc<br /> Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd change it to look more like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i>Electrification Domain</i></b></span><br /> &quot;Sweet quote about lightning/divinity.&quot;<br /> Fancy words explaining the purview of these Transmutations<br /> <br /> <b><i>Chaac's Wrath Transmutations</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Shock - Minor</i><br /> Words go here.<br /> <br /> <i>Arc - Major</i><br /> Words.<br /> <br /> <i>Divine Lightning - Supernal</i><br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Thor's Benediction Transmutations</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Insulator - Minor</i><br /> Words go here.<br /> <br /> <i>Power Sink - Major</i><br /> Words.<br /> <br /> <i>Lightning Therapy - Supernal</i><br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Zeus' Might Transmutations</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Jolt - Minor</i><br /> Words go here.<br /> <br /> <i>Generator - Major</i><br /> Words.<br /> <br /> <i>Regulator - Supernal</i><br /> Etc. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T13:15:31-07:00","id":149690,"title":"","content":"Non Abrahmaic and non Greek theology in Promethian; I'm not so sure about that. I know you have things like the Osirens, but the Divine Fire / Transmutations themselves have always been heavily based on Greek/Abhamaic (there's a lot of cross-influence) ideas.<br /> <br /> I'd use Zeus for the Divine Lighting tree; but not the other gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:23:49-07:00","id":149984,"title":"","content":"Though I know where you're coming from, I'd remove mythological references from the masthead like that.<br /> Reasons:<br /> 1. Those thing's King's Raven said.<br /> <br /> 2. We can go absolutely insane with Alchemical, Planetary and Scientific references, too; we can build a system around all that, but that adds a layer of complexity that I don't think it behooves us to consider until we actually have solid system (read: one that will work) down.<br /> We can get more mileage out of Qaballah, too.<br /> <br /> 3. We would have to do this for every Transmutation set. I love mythology; I know a lot of mythology (like, a lot). The idea of shoe-horning in mythological references does not appeal to me.<br /> <br /> 4. What does this add, that simply using already-extant Transmutations does not?<br /> Here's what I mean: <br /> What does Chaac's Wrath (nice call-out, by the way) add to the game as a name-set for powers that simply having it say &quot;Divine Lightning&quot; doesn't already do?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm still partial to having it say &quot;Electrification Transmutations&quot; and then just, naming each one after the top of the tree. Or naming each one based on what it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My reservations about this system still exist. They are:<br /> 1. &quot;Blackout&quot; isn't on there.<br /> 2. How do we work in 1-5 dot?<br /> <br /> My solutions:<br /> 1. &quot;Blackout&quot; and others like it have Minor/Major Transmutations as prerequisites, from separate trees; Blackout would require &quot;Insulator&quot; and &quot;Jolt&quot; and probably be Major, for instance.<br /> 2. We have a second sub-type of Transmutation called &quot;Alterations&quot; that would be for stuff like Might, Perfected Reflexes, Hard Body, Alembic, and so on. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I <i>like</i> these solutions, especially since they work together - you can have standard Mi --&gt; Ma --&gt; Su Transmutations be prerequisites alongside Alterations for those in-between or hard-to-define ones.<br /> Also, it still makes Synergies easier to make.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T21:08:49-07:00","id":150010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I know where you're coming from, I'd remove mythological references from the masthead like that.<br /> Reasons:<br /> 1. Those thing's King's Raven said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I guess I just got too much into the Divinity thingy while completely leaving behind the Greek myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. We can go absolutely insane with Alchemical, Planetary and Scientific references, too; we can build a system around all that, but that adds a layer of complexity that I don't think it behooves us to consider until we actually have solid system (read: one that will work) down.<br /> We can get more mileage out of Qaballah, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you're right, but I think it's easier to work on projects like these (read: large &quot;folder&quot; quantity) when they are nicely categorized rather than when they are named &quot;power 34&quot;. Also, my programming background has some weird effects on my workflow that wants me to name and categorize everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. We would have to do this for every Transmutation set. I love mythology; I know a lot of mythology (like, a lot). The idea of shoe-horning in mythological references does not appeal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, it's mainly your project after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I respect this decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. What does this add, that simply using already-extant Transmutations does not?<br /> Here's what I mean:<br /> What does Chaac's Wrath (nice call-out, by the way) add to the game as a name-set for powers that simply having it say &quot;Divine Lightning&quot; doesn't already do?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm still partial to having it say &quot;Electrification Transmutations&quot; and then just, naming each one after the top of the tree. Or naming each one based on what it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>It adds nothing, but I think that &quot;Divine Lightning&quot; does not fit the whole &quot;I can throw lightning AND infuse my attacks!!! RAWR!&quot;. I would still like it to be changed to something else, mythological or not. Also, I don't think we need to name every level of a Transmutation, but that is to be discussed further and later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reservations about this system still exist. They are:<br /> 1. &quot;Blackout&quot; isn't on there.<br /> 2. How do we work in 1-5 dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we really need to work them in? Or can we simply work them as &quot;shadow gifts&quot; that are approximatelly 3-dots in power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My solutions:<br /> 1. &quot;Blackout&quot; and others like it have Minor/Major Transmutations as prerequisites, from separate trees; Blackout would require &quot;Insulator&quot; and &quot;Jolt&quot; and probably be Major, for instance.<br /> 2. We have a second sub-type of Transmutation called &quot;Alterations&quot; that would be for stuff like Might, Perfected Reflexes, Hard Body, Alembic, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I....have nothing to say here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I <i>like</i> these solutions, especially since they work together - you can have standard Mi --&gt; Ma --&gt; Su Transmutations be prerequisites alongside Alterations for those in-between or hard-to-define ones.<br /> Also, it still makes Synergies easier to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am eager to work on Synergies, I think it will be the thing that was missing from this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149984#post149984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need another beer, a day off and some hours to work on this. Also, we should decide which transmutations to keep and which to throw out the window, and we'll probably need to work the MO transmutations too at some point...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T21:19:04-07:00","id":150019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/138687-another-round-at-gmc?p=149666#post149666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a quote used in Genius: the Transgression. It's more metaphorical than literal:<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is the lightning to lick you with its tongue? Where is the madness with which you should be cleansed?<br /> Behold, I show you the Superman. He is this lightning, he is this madness.&quot;<br /> -Friedrich Nietzsche, Thus Spoke Zarathustra</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right<br /> I finally have a good reason to bust out all my Philosophy texts.<br /> Best pet project ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T11:22:28-07:00","id":150608,"title":"","content":"He's one for the Alchemicus. From one of the best games ever; but also a really really obscure mod. Penny would probably make a much better Sin-Eater than Promethean though.<br /> <br /> Psalm 92, uranium. free me, Penny! free me and I will serve you.<br /> I can do no more. remember my psalms Penny- call 13-29-5-92-16<br /> Thank you, Penny. together we will change everything. you are the mortar, and I am the pestle<br /> I am AlCuBUS. I will write you a book of changes like the world has never seen<br /> I am inside you Penny. Nothing can ever be the same again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-27-2014, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:13:48-07:00","id":153343,"title":"","content":"What game is that from. Because that's amazing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more on topic: I've been toying with an Integrity system called Restraint (bear with me a second). Restraint has no <i>natural</i> Breaking Points; you set some appropriate to your character but otherwise... pretty tough to lose it accidentally.<br /> <br /> No, you lose it <i>intentionally</i>. You can choose, whenever you make a roll, to make reflexively make a Breaking Point roll against Restraint, with a penalty from -1 to -5. Each -1 of penalty you take adds a die to the original roll; however, failing the Breaking Point smacks you with some consequence for letting loose, for being <i>weak</i>. It was for a Wuxia splat concept, to emulate stuff like Billy Jack going BEE-ZERK.<br /> <br /> But anyway... I think Prometheans might be able to benefit from that. Maybe not that <i>precise</i> benefit, but they should get <i>some</i> incentive for backsliding. Risk a Breaking Point to get some substantive bonuses; come on, give in to the fact that you're nothing but a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T19:41:51-07:00","id":153406,"title":"","content":"They already have that.<br /> They're called &quot;Pandoran Transmutations,&quot; and if you're a Centimanus, using them doesn't prompt a Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T19:57:52-07:00","id":153418,"title":"","content":"Heh. Forgot about those <i>completely.</i><br /> <br /> Carry on, good sirs/madams/unaffiliated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:07:09-07:00","id":161903,"title":"","content":"Hey<br /> <br /> So Magnum Opus and I are slowly yet surely working out a new Transmutation system; in the meantime, I'm trying to update the RAW Transmutations so they're more GMC-y. They still have dot ratings, and I'm mostly writing notes that should be compared to the book. I'd love some input on my changes, though; make sure I've got a proper balance.<br /> I am always worried about balance. All the time. Forever. Curse you, Zoroastrian dreams.<br /> I'm roughly comparing them to &quot;Blood &amp; Smoke,&quot; with an eye towards 1-dot Transmutations being useful but not overly game-breaking, two-dot being similar to some Discipline powers, and then ranging up from there.<br /> <br /> I also intend to write in fixes where the rules seem to be mega-borked or unintentionally complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:28:23-07:00","id":161922,"title":"","content":"Want me to get in on this? For the first time in forever I don't seem to have many projects on my plate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}